## 7. Feature-Level Target State

Runtime should expose a coherent durable execution model: sessions bind user, agent, environment, memory, runs, steps, tool calls, model calls, checkpoints, artifacts, and traces. Persistence should record event history and activity results. Workers should recover after process failure and avoid duplicated side effects. APIs and SDKs should make session/run operations first class. Observability should show timeline, status, replay, checkpoint, policy, and artifact evidence in one view. Tests should prove crash recovery, replay, idempotency, and trace linkage.

